trajectory.patch:
`onoff_reset` function in `lib/utils/onoff.c` incorrectly returns early if `validate_args` succeeds (returns 0). The condition `if (rv <= 0)` should only trigger for negative error codes, not for a successful validation. This causes `onoff_reset` to return `0` (which corresponds to `ONOFF_STATE_OFF`) instead of the actual manager state (`ONOFF_STATE_ERROR`) when a reset is initiated from an error state.

The fix changes the condition to `if (rv < 0)` to correctly handle the return value of `validate_args`.

